# Agent pull requests (contributor identity)

Agents open PRs as a **dedicated GitHub contributor**, not as the repo owner’s personal account.

## Auth

- Prefer `GH_TOKEN` (or `GITHUB_TOKEN`) for a **machine / bot user** with write access to this repo.
- Prefer HTTPS `origin` (`https://github.com/vctrch/GolfGps_Android.git`) so token auth works.
- Load local secrets from `.cursor/agent.env` when present (gitignored). Never commit tokens.
- If `GH_TOKEN` is unset and `gh` / push fails, stop and tell the human to finish [Agent GitHub setup](agent-github-setup.md) — do not use their personal SSH key as a substitute “fix”.

## Identity on commits

When creating commits that will be pushed for an agent PR, set author/committer for that commit only (no `git config`):

```bash
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME="CommunityGolf Agent"
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL="communitygolf-agent@users.noreply.github.com"
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME="CommunityGolf Agent"
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL="communitygolf-agent@users.noreply.github.com"
```

Use the real bot account’s noreply email once the machine user exists (update this rule if the login changes).

## PR workflow

1. Branch from the requested base (often `develop` or a feature branch).
2. Commit only with user approval (or when they asked to submit a PR).
3. `git push -u origin HEAD` then `gh pr create --base <base>`.
4. Return the PR URL.
5. Do not merge unless asked.

## Safety

- Never force-push shared branches (`main`, `master`, `develop`).
- Never put PATs, `.cursor/agent.env`, or key material in the repo or PR body.
